# /public/build is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# The production host is shared hosting with no node, so it cannot run the
# build itself — which makes the compiled bundle a deployment artefact rather
# than a working file. Ignoring it meant every release had to be scp'd by
# hand, and Windows scp writes directories as 700, so the stylesheet 404'd
# while the pages themselves loaded fine. Twice.
#
# Committing it costs a noisy diff on every asset change and buys a deploy
# that is `git pull` and nothing else. On a host that could run `npm ci`, take
# this back out.

